# REVIEW.md

<!--
Template for a repository's REVIEW.md. Copy it to REVIEW.md (or
.claude/REVIEW.md) at the repository root and edit it. /ccmagic:review reads
it from the merge base of the change under review, so an edit to this file
takes effect for changes made after it merges, never for the PR that makes it.

CLAUDE.md says how to write code here. REVIEW.md says what matters when
reviewing it. Keep it short: the good ones fit on one screen.

The four sections below are the ones the review skill acts on. Any other
section is passed to every reviewer as guidance, as written.
-->

## Failure modes

What a bad change looks like in this repository. Reviewers look for these
first. A finding that is one of them is raised to the severity named here, or
one level when none is named.

- Docs: it lies. A doc, comment, or help text that describes behavior the
  code does not have is High.
- Config: it misroutes. A route, queue name, or environment key that sends
  traffic or data to the wrong place is Critical.
- Migrations: they lock or lose data on a large table.

## Skip

Paths the reviewer does not read. One glob per list item. `*` stays within a
directory, `**` crosses directories, a trailing `/` means everything under that
directory, and a glob without a `/` matches at any depth.

- `src/generated/**` generated API client
- `vendor/`
- `*.snap`
- `package-lock.json`

## Nit cap

3

## Evidence

Every finding cites a file and line, never a guess from a name. A Critical
finding also gives the command or input that reproduces it.
